1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,801
Aarav brakes his bike.

2
00:00:01,801 --> 00:00:03,857
A ceiling fan spins above his desk.

3
00:00:03,857 --> 00:00:06,083
He carries his books down the corridor.

4
00:00:06,483 --> 00:00:08,680
Three forces, three moving things.

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,261
But very different work.

6
00:00:10,711 --> 00:00:13,599
The fan's motor pushes each
blade along its circle.

7
00:00:13,599 --> 00:00:15,636
The brakes push back on the bike.

8
00:00:15,636 --> 00:00:18,085
His hands hold the books up as he walks.

9
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:23,026
One force does positive work, one
does negative work, and one does none.

10
00:00:23,026 --> 00:00:24,394
Can you match them?

11
00:00:24,894 --> 00:00:26,984
Work is F d cos theta.

12
00:00:27,334 --> 00:00:29,824
F and d are sizes, never negative.

13
00:00:29,824 --> 00:00:32,475
So the sign comes only from cos theta.

14
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:37,525
Force along the motion: theta is under
ninety, cos theta is positive, so

15
00:00:37,525 --> 00:00:39,039
the work is positive.

16
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:40,249
The force helps.

17
00:00:40,649 --> 00:00:45,093
Force against the motion: theta is
over ninety, cos theta is negative,

18
00:00:45,093 --> 00:00:46,795
so the work is negative.

19
00:00:46,795 --> 00:00:48,040
The force fights.

20
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:51,258
At exactly ninety degrees,
cos theta is zero.

21
00:00:51,258 --> 00:00:52,393
No work at all.

22
00:00:53,043 --> 00:00:55,201
Let's see all three on Aarav's bike ride.

23
00:00:55,201 --> 00:00:57,262
Aarav and his bike: eighty kilograms.

24
00:00:57,612 --> 00:00:58,871
First, he pedals.

25
00:00:58,871 --> 00:01:02,100
A forward push of forty
newtons, over sixteen metres.

26
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:05,475
Along the motion, so plus
six hundred and forty joules.

27
00:01:05,875 --> 00:01:08,483
Then he cruises at four metres per second.

28
00:01:08,483 --> 00:01:10,713
No push, no brakes, so no work.

29
00:01:11,113 --> 00:01:12,104
Now he brakes.

30
00:01:12,104 --> 00:01:15,255
A backward force of eighty
newtons, over eight metres.

31
00:01:15,255 --> 00:01:17,327
Minus six hundred and forty joules.

32
00:01:17,727 --> 00:01:22,110
All along, the road pushes up and
gravity pulls down, at ninety degrees

33
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:23,191
to the motion.

34
00:01:23,191 --> 00:01:24,091
Zero work.

35
00:01:24,524 --> 00:01:26,473
Slow-mo replay of the braking.

36
00:01:26,823 --> 00:01:28,864
The bike moves forward along d.

37
00:01:28,864 --> 00:01:30,894
The brake force points backward.

38
00:01:30,894 --> 00:01:34,351
Theta is one eighty, and
cos one eighty is minus one.

39
00:01:34,851 --> 00:01:39,324
On the graph, the push line climbs,
the brake line falls, and the up and

40
00:01:39,324 --> 00:01:40,984
down forces stay at zero.

41
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:43,725
Now the rule, one step at a time.

42
00:01:44,075 --> 00:01:45,034
Step one.

43
00:01:45,034 --> 00:01:49,381
W equals F d cos theta, with
F and d always positive.

44
00:01:50,131 --> 00:01:51,031
Step two.

45
00:01:50,893 --> 00:01:52,603
Theta under ninety degrees.

46
00:01:52,603 --> 00:01:55,232
Cos theta is positive, so W is positive.

47
00:01:55,982 --> 00:01:56,962
Step three.

48
00:01:56,962 --> 00:01:58,540
Theta exactly ninety.

49
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,130
Cos theta is zero, so W is zero.

50
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,810
Step four.

51
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:04,231
Theta over ninety.

52
00:02:04,231 --> 00:02:07,255
Cos theta is negative, so W is negative.

53
00:02:07,255 --> 00:02:09,744
At one eighty, W is minus F d.

54
00:02:10,494 --> 00:02:11,482
Remember this.

55
00:02:11,482 --> 00:02:13,419
Positive work helps the motion.

56
00:02:13,419 --> 00:02:14,978
Negative work fights it.

57
00:02:14,978 --> 00:02:16,491
Zero work does neither.

58
00:02:17,191 --> 00:02:18,612
Now, side by side.

59
00:02:18,962 --> 00:02:22,096
Push a moving swing
forward, along its motion.

60
00:02:22,096 --> 00:02:23,227
Theta is zero.

61
00:02:23,227 --> 00:02:24,299
Positive work.

62
00:02:24,699 --> 00:02:26,008
Catch a fast ball.

63
00:02:26,008 --> 00:02:28,768
It moves toward you, your hands push back.

64
00:02:28,768 --> 00:02:30,172
Theta is one eighty.

65
00:02:30,172 --> 00:02:31,915
Negative work on the ball.

66
00:02:32,515 --> 00:02:33,426
Now you try.

67
00:02:33,426 --> 00:02:36,709
Diya lowers a bucket into
a well, slowly, on a rope.

68
00:02:36,709 --> 00:02:39,258
The rope pulls up, the bucket moves down.

69
00:02:39,258 --> 00:02:42,116
Is the rope's work
positive, negative, or zero?

70
00:02:42,116 --> 00:02:43,205
Pause and think.

71
00:02:46,405 --> 00:02:47,305
Negative!

72
00:02:47,110 --> 00:02:49,783
The rope pulls up, the bucket moves down.

73
00:02:49,783 --> 00:02:51,593
Theta is one eighty degrees.

74
00:02:52,243 --> 00:02:53,148
Now the fan.

75
00:02:53,148 --> 00:02:56,831
Why does the pull that keeps a
blade on its circle do no work?

76
00:02:56,831 --> 00:02:57,957
Follow the links.

77
00:02:58,307 --> 00:02:59,207
One.

78
00:02:58,758 --> 00:03:01,680
The blade tip moves along
the edge of its circle.

79
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,980
Two.

80
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:05,429
The pull that keeps it on the
circle points to the centre.

81
00:03:05,829 --> 00:03:06,729
Three.

82
00:03:06,357 --> 00:03:09,884
A line to the centre is always
at ninety degrees to the edge.

83
00:03:09,884 --> 00:03:11,968
So theta is ninety, every instant.

84
00:03:12,368 --> 00:03:13,268
Four.

85
00:03:12,939 --> 00:03:17,935
Cos ninety is zero, so the inward
pull does no work, all the way round.

86
00:03:18,335 --> 00:03:19,963
So, Aarav's three forces.

87
00:03:19,963 --> 00:03:21,591
The fan motor, positive.

88
00:03:21,591 --> 00:03:23,028
The brakes, negative.

89
00:03:23,028 --> 00:03:24,992
His hands on the books, zero.

90
00:03:25,642 --> 00:03:27,332
Now, one worked example.

91
00:03:27,682 --> 00:03:32,024
A box is pulled three metres across a
floor, by a ten newton force at sixty

92
00:03:32,024 --> 00:03:32,924
degrees.

93
00:03:32,659 --> 00:03:34,258
Friction is three newtons.

94
00:03:34,258 --> 00:03:36,330
Find the work done by each force.

95
00:03:36,830 --> 00:03:37,730
The pull.

96
00:03:37,647 --> 00:03:40,764
Ten, times three, times cos sixty, a half.

97
00:03:40,764 --> 00:03:42,189
Plus fifteen joules.

98
00:03:42,939 --> 00:03:45,789
Friction points backward,
theta one eighty.

99
00:03:45,789 --> 00:03:48,240
Three times three, times minus one.

100
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,566
Minus nine joules.

101
00:03:50,316 --> 00:03:53,443
Gravity and the normal
force are at ninety degrees.

102
00:03:53,443 --> 00:03:54,642
Zero, and zero.

103
00:03:55,392 --> 00:03:58,663
In total, fifteen minus nine, six joules.

104
00:03:59,313 --> 00:04:00,774
Now, the exam trap.

105
00:04:01,124 --> 00:04:05,325
Many students think negative work
means work done backwards, as if work

106
00:04:05,325 --> 00:04:06,493
had a direction.

107
00:04:06,843 --> 00:04:08,439
But work is a scalar.

108
00:04:08,439 --> 00:04:11,979
The minus sign only says the
force opposes the motion.

109
00:04:12,629 --> 00:04:14,076
Where is this asked?

110
00:04:14,076 --> 00:04:18,972
The sign of the work done by gravity,
friction, the normal force and tension,

111
00:04:18,972 --> 00:04:20,274
often on a slope.

112
00:04:20,874 --> 00:04:22,104
Exam level now.

113
00:04:22,104 --> 00:04:26,720
A two kilogram block slides five
metres down a rough thirty seven degree

114
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:27,620
slope.

115
00:04:27,355 --> 00:04:31,711
Mu is point five, g is ten,
sine thirty seven is point six.

116
00:04:31,711 --> 00:04:35,941
Find the work done by gravity,
friction and the normal force.

117
00:04:35,941 --> 00:04:37,223
Pause and solve.

118
00:04:42,623 --> 00:04:43,946
The answer is A.

119
00:04:43,946 --> 00:04:46,622
Sixty, minus forty, and zero joules.

120
00:04:47,122 --> 00:04:52,034
Gravity along the slope is m g sine
theta, twelve newtons, along the motion.

121
00:04:52,034 --> 00:04:53,317
Plus sixty joules.

122
00:04:53,817 --> 00:04:58,030
Friction is mu m g cos theta,
eight newtons, against the motion.

123
00:04:58,030 --> 00:04:59,361
Minus forty joules.

124
00:04:59,861 --> 00:05:02,279
The normal force is at ninety degrees.

125
00:05:02,279 --> 00:05:03,179
Zero.

126
00:05:03,406 --> 00:05:04,947
Here is your recap.

127
00:05:04,947 --> 00:05:06,531
Screenshot this card.

128
00:05:09,731 --> 00:05:11,917
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

129
00:05:12,317 --> 00:05:13,217
One.

130
00:05:12,779 --> 00:05:14,551
F and d are never negative.

131
00:05:14,551 --> 00:05:16,315
So what makes work negative?

132
00:05:17,215 --> 00:05:18,115
Two.

133
00:05:17,657 --> 00:05:20,703
Why does the inward pull
on a fan blade do no work?

134
00:05:21,603 --> 00:05:22,503
Three.

135
00:05:22,117 --> 00:05:26,289
When Diya lowers the bucket, what is
the sign of the work done by gravity?

136
00:05:27,389 --> 00:05:31,708
Next time: stretch a rubber band,
and it pulls back harder and harder.

137
00:05:31,708 --> 00:05:34,767
How do we find work when
the force keeps changing?

138
00:05:34,767 --> 00:05:37,597
We find out in work done
by a variable force.
